## 6. Validation ladder (each rung logged with commands and outputs)

1. static (`py_compile`, `bash -n`, `git diff --check`); 2. `pytest tests/` (all existing tests plus the new ones); 3. tiny synthetic forward with `--yaw-aug 1` (finite loss, gradients flow); 4. real-data readback on 50 batches: depth roll exact, source and reference distances unchanged, target and reference audio unchanged, **alignment audit** by `tools/yaw_aug.alignment_audit(batches, offsets, model)` (integer delays only, computed with the model's own `shift_and_align` on the GPU in float32 exactly as in training, for the rotated versus the un-rotated geometry; cohort = the first 50 micro-batches of epoch 1 with their counter offsets; artefact `alignment_audit.json` with the cohort digest (query paths + offsets), the changed-delay count and the denominator 12 800; reviewed with round 1); 5. smoke (exact argv, same environment and interpreter as the full run): `python train_xRIR_backbone.py --backbone simple --save-dir <attempt>/smoke --num-shot 8 --max-len 9600 --lr 1e-3 --weight-decay 1e-4 --decay-epochs 3 --lr-gamma 0.1 --epochs 1 --max-train-batches 3 --max-test-batches 2 --batch-size 4 --accum-steps 2 --num-workers 4 --seed 0 --tf32 --log-interval 1 --save-every 0 --epoch-ckpt-every 0 --no-save --yaw-aug 1 --yaw-aug-seed 0 --yaw-aug-width 512` (banner, three finite steps, nothing written); 6. throughput probe: 50 micro-batches at 32 × 2 with and without augmentation on the target GPU, overhead > 5 % blocks the launch; 7. parity audit: `--yaw-aug 0` loss on the first real batch equals the exp_01 script's loss bit for bit (same seed); type-strict diff of the launcher's pre-spawn `effective_args.json` against the control's `args.json`, excluding only `save_dir`, the three yaw keys, `no_save`, `PYTHONHASHSEED` and the cadence keys (`save_every`, `epoch_ckpt_every`), with every excluded difference listed in the notebook; 8. final integrative Codex review of the whole diff; 9. full run through a fail-closed launcher (`launch_yaw_aug.sh`: exact argv, source/data identity, empty output directory, free GPU and disk, banner flushed before step one, teed timestamped log).

